<ul>
<li>40, 40 → RANK 1, 1, then the 35-hour row gets <strong>3</strong> (two people are ahead of it). DENSE_RANK gives it <strong>2</strong> (one distinct value is ahead).</li>
<li>ROW_NUMBER numbers 1…16 no matter what — so its ORDER BY must be <strong>unique</strong>, otherwise the two 40-hour rows may swap between runs. Here <code>w.empSSN, w.proNum</code> (the primary key) breaks every tie.</li>
</ul>
